  "EntityComments": [
    {
      "EntityName": "dxtask",
      "EntityCopyID": "0839b1d9-499e-4b33-a5b5-8c4d12f6e4bc",
      "CommentData": "<p>Illustrates the standard multi-branch fan-in pattern: a trivial <strong>Split</strong> root step (Bulk, returns <code>[]</code>) that every parallel branch chains off via <code>PrevStepCopyID</code>, then a <strong>Merge results</strong> step (also Bulk, plus <code>AdditionalInputs</code> from every branch) that fans them back into one output. Branch A nests a RowByRowSequentially step under its own Bulk generator (3-segment address), Branch B stays flat (2-segment address) - see docs/entities/data-addressing.md.</p>",
      "CreatedByName": "Integray",
      "ModifiedByName": "Integray"
    },
    {
      "EntityName": "dxschema",
      "EntityCopyID": "ec55ed3a-a167-4f36-90dc-c3b20516826a",
      "CommentData": "<p>Illustrates a <code>Type:7</code> (Table) column with <code>ComplexType</code> pointing at a sub-schema (<strong>Sample Item</strong>, also present in <code>DataSchemas[]</code>) \u2014 see docs/transfer/config-transfer-format.md \u00a77. Declared standalone here, not wired into any Step/Task in this example.</p>",
      "CreatedByName": "Integray",
      "ModifiedByName": "Integray"
    },
    {
      "EntityName": "dxtask",
      "EntityCopyID": "e827affe-362c-4eea-9461-c7fdad77736e",
      "CommentData": "<p>Illustrates three mechanisms not covered by the other tasks: <strong>Data Checkpoint</strong> (<code>DataStorageColumn</code> on the Node.js processor step - see docs/entities/data-checkpoint.md), <strong>Local Variables</strong> (<code>VariablesSchema</code>/<code>VariablesDefaults</code> on the Task, written via <code>VariablesSchemaMapping</code> and read back via the <code>${LocalVariable.Label}</code> placeholder - see docs/entities/local-variables.md), and a top-level <strong>Variable</strong> referenced via <code>${#DemoApiToken}</code> - see docs/entities/variables.md. Also the only task in this example using the <strong>Node.js processor</strong> connector instead of JS Mapper.</p>",
      "CreatedByName": "Integray",
      "ModifiedByName": "Integray"
    },
    {
      "EntityName": "dxendpoint",
      "EntityCopyID": "4f7c7ed9-b95d-43aa-a3bb-aadff435a322",
      "CommentData": "<p>⚠️ <strong>WARNING - REAL TOKEN VALUE, NOT A PLACEHOLDER.</strong> Every <code>*Token</code> field here and the <code>SecondaryTokens[]</code> entry are set to <code>rnE9TBvaDso=</code> - a real, working self-test token value (encrypted/at-rest form; its plaintext counterpart, used in the <code>Authorization: Bearer ...</code> header, is the literal string <code>Token 1</code> - see <code>docs/transfer/config-transfer-format.md §8.2</code> and docs/transfer/config-transfer-format.md §8.2). It is illustrative of the encrypted-vs-plaintext gotcha, <strong>not a safe secret</strong> - anyone who has read this file knows it. <strong>Generate and substitute your own token before using this endpoint for anything real.</strong></p>",
      "CreatedByName": "Integray",
      "ModifiedByName": "Integray"
    }
  ],
